            <ArticleTitle>Clinical inquiries: What measures relieve postherpetic neuralgia?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>384d-f</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>EVIDENCE-BASED ANSWER: Tricyclic antidepressants, gabapentin, and pregabalin effectively reduce pain. Opioids have demonstrated pain relief in 3 RCTs. Capsaicin and the lidocaine 5% patch relieve pain and decrease allodynia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
